<!--Post: 3439--><!--Time: 1104896603-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nancy worked at helzberg jewelry store before her death. Is it possible that BTK met her there while purchasing or shopping for a  wedding/engagement ring? After her murder there were no more for about 8 years. I was wondering if there was a way too check marriage/engagement announcements up to about 6 months prior to her death. And then Divorces from 85 and 86, prior to Vicki Wegerle&#39;s death. Maybe There would be a match that would fit the profile of BTK. I know that it is an incredible reach. BUt it would explain why BTK was not heard from for several years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3439-->
<!--Post: 3620--><!--Time: 1105068155-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3620"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 7:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nancy Fox worked at Helzberg Jewellers the night of her death. She went right from work to home and was probably killed soon after entering her home. <BR>This murder stands out to me a something special to BTK. <BR>It is the only murder that BTK reports himself with his phone call reporting the homocide of Nancy Fox. He knew she lived alone and had few friends other than work and he wanted her body found right away. <BR>Her co-worker at Helzberg&#39;s Julie Ladd had been stabbed to death a few months earlier at WSU. A man confessed to her murder and is currently serving time in a Colorado prison. Not that BTK had anything to do with Ladd&#39;s murder but he would have known about it and an upsetting event like that would have of course caused Fox to discuss it with many people she came in contact with. <BR>The pearl and gold necklace that was among her missing possessions and is now being sought by investigators. Did Fox buy this necklace from her work at Helzberg&#39;s or was it a gift to her from someone? Why did BTK feel the need to take this piece of jewelery? Could BTK have been a customer at her store? <BR>Fox&#39;s purse was found emptied and it&#39;s contents spilled on a coffee table. Her drivers license was missing and is found recently placed in a plastic bag in a park with some of her other possessions 27 years later. Why? <BR>She worked full-time for a construction company and between her two jobs was in contact with a lot of the general public everyday. Could BTK have been a client or a laborer at one time of the construction company? <BR>Her murder was the only nightime killing of BTK although the Anna Williams attempt would have happened at night while BTK waited for her to return home. Why not kill her in the morning before she went to work? She lived alone so no one else would have been there. Her work could have possibly sent someone to look for her once she failed to report for work and he didn&#39;t want to be caught or have to hurry his killing before someone eventually came around to look for her so he wanted a maximum ammount of time to spend with this victim. All night if he needed to fully enjoy this killing. Why? As it turned out no one from her work  ever had to eventually go looking for her as BTK himself reported her death at 8:20 the next morning. <BR>BTK sends an almost professionally crime lab detailed sketch of Fox&#39;s crime scene to the media and inspires him to become a poet by sending his version of a traditional folk song along with his discription of the crime. <BR>At 25 she was within the probable comtempory age of BTK. She graduated from South High School in Wichita in 1970. In all probability BTK himself was a long-time resident of Wichita. Did he attend South High School himself? Did he know her from back in high school days. She would have attended there between the Fall of 1966 and Spring of 1970. Did BTK attend that same school during those years? Maybe being a member of the one of the classes of 1967,1968,1969 or 1970. <BR>Was this more than seeking, stalking and killing a victim? Did BTK personally know Nancy Fox? <BR>Bulldog87 offers a plausable scenario of BTK possibly purchasing an engagement or wedding ring at Helzerg&#39;s. Maybe he went there to have his watch repaired that he stole from Mr. Otero years earlier.    <BR>I think there is more to the Fox murder than a random stalk and kill. I think BTK knew Nancy Fox.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3620-->
<!--Post: 3635--><!--Time: 1105076391-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3635"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am pretty convinced that BTK knew Miss Fox and also knew Joseph Otero and possibly all of the other victims.  <BR>Have WPD or the FBI ever actually examined commonalities between all 8 of the known &#40;there are almost certainly unknown&#41; victims and excluded a common connection positively?  <BR>I also find the Coleman production line connection interesting, as is Mr. Otero&#39;s military service. There had to be some kind of connection somewhere. The BTK murders were way too passionate and well planned to be simply random murders of strangers, particularly in the case of the Oteros.  <BR>Based on what Charlie Otero has said about his father&#39;s behavior in the days prior to the murders, there is a real possibility that Mr. Otero was fearful of something or someone, of some imminent clear and present danger to his family. Is it possible that BTK committed a crime that was witnessed by Mr. Otero, or that Mr. Otero saw or heard or knew something in the military that he was pretty sure someone would kill to keep secret? Charlie Otero has said on several occasions that he belives his father knew BTK and also knew that a threat to his family was potentially imminent &#40;checking for the lights being out elsewhere during a power failure before letting the kids out of a closet, having Charlie look out the window for a service truck before opening the door to a serviceman, etc.&#41; Charlie also said something in one particular interview that has flown pretty much completely under the radar but is remarkable - he said that he was told that his father, during the course of the Otero homicides, was UNbound and forced to write something down before being REbound and killed. I don&#39;t remember exactly when Charlie Otero said that, but IF it is accurate it is very disturbing since it indicates that BTK both knew Mr. Otero and also had some kind of connection with him that was a secret worth killing an entire family over &#40;another possibility is that perhaps BTK forced Mr. Otero, by threatening his children and wife, to sign over something of value or importance&#41;. Granted, Charlie Otero has not always been 100% consistent in his statements, so this is possibly not accurate. Does anyone KNOW if it is one way or the other?  <BR>I believe it is silly to think that BTK did NOT know his victims SOMEHOW. Discovering what that common connection is seems to me to be something that would shed condsiderable light on who BTK is and why the murders, especially the Oteros, occured in the first place. Hopefully someday we will know what was behind BTK&#39;s selection of the victims he picked.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3635-->
<!--Post: 3663--><!--Time: 1105112594-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3663"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 7:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Did they all have library cards or frequent the library? <BR> <BR>I have always thought there is a library conection.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3663-->
<!--Post: 3664--><!--Time: 1105113335-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3664"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 7:55 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva, <BR> <BR>I may have misunderstood, but your comment about Charlie Otero&#39;s statement doesn&#39;t make sense. You stated that Charlie said his father was &#34;UNbound and forced to write something down&#34;. How would Charlie know this when he wasn&#39;t there at the time?  <BR> <BR>Charlie returned from school to find his family murdered. Please try to find the statement as I&#39;m sure you didn&#39;t make it up. I am curious to know what was misunderstood. <BR> <BR>iq<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3664-->
<!--Post: 3682--><!--Time: 1105128147-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3682"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is turning into an Otero discussion...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3682-->
<!--Post: 4134--><!--Time: 1105733492-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4134"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cricket<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cricket<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iq -  <BR> <BR>The statement Charlie Otero made that his father was unbound is in a link found at: <BR>The Nancy Fox Phone Call discussion &#40;the one before this one&#41;- Writen by Beck 1/12/05 at 12:06 pm. <BR> <BR>But in this link it says Charlie Otero also said he walked in his parents room and they were lying side by side on the bed.  So I don&#39;t really give this much credit.  Interesting link though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
